        "original_id": "6b7c8c96-16f8-5088-b93b-1cf1ac8f1c04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: The Venetian Macao, The Venetian Las Vegas, Macau\n- Organizations: KlingStubbins, 10th IIFA Awards\n- Concepts: building floor area, hotel tower design\n\nFacts:\n- The Venetian Macao is modeled on its sister casino resort, The Venetian Las Vegas.\n- The Venetian Macao has 10,500,000 square feet of floor area and is the seventh-largest building in the world by floor area.\n- The hotel tower at The Venetian Las Vegas was designed by KlingStubbins.\n- The hotel tower at The Venetian Las Vegas contains 36 stories and rises 475 feet.\n- The 10th IIFA Awards ceremony was held at The Venetian Macao in Macau from June 11 to June 13, 2009.",
